    "ExplanationCorrect": "DuPont ROE = net profit margin x asset turnover x equity multiplier. Current ROE = 0.068 x 1.40 x 1.75 = 0.0952 x 1.75 = 0.1666, rounded to 16.7%. Prior ROE = 0.058 x 1.30 = 0.0754; 0.0754 x 1.79 = 0.1350 = 13.5% which checks. Change = +3.2 percentage points. Attribution: margin contributed +1.75 points (1.0% absolute margin rise x prior turnover and leverage), turnover +0.90 points, leverage -0.45 points (decline from 1.79 to 1.75 reduces ROE). Margin is the largest contributor, leverage slightly offsets the operational improvement, so the ROE rise is fundamentally operational. Recomputed independently: 0.068 x 1.40 = 0.0952; 0.0952 x 1.75 = 0.1666 = 16.7%; prior 0.058 x 1.30 = 0.0754; 0.0754 x 1.79 = 13.5%. Business interpretation: Senior analyst Priya Ramaswamy should tell the board the ROE improvement reflects operating gains (margin and efficiency), not riskier leverage, so the higher return is more sustainable than a leverage-driven spike. The trap is misattributing the driver to leverage or averaging.",
    "ExplanationWrongA": "Choice A understates current ROE at 14.2% and misattributes the driver to leverage. The misconception is using prior-year turnover with current margin or mis-applying the multiplier; leverage actually fell from 1.79 to 1.75 and reduced ROE by about 0.45 points, so correct ROE is 0.068 x 1.40 x 1.75 = 16.7% driven by margin, which is Choice C, not A.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Choice B misstates ROE by computing 15.5% using prior turnover 1.30. The misconception is substituting prior turnover 1.30 x 0.068 x 1.75 = 15.5%; correct turnover is 1.40, so ROE is 0.068 x 1.40 x 1.75 = 16.7% with margin as the largest driver, which is Choice C.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Choice D overstates ROE to 18.1% by multiplying margin, turnover, and leverage additively or using inflated inputs. The misconception is summing components rather than multiplying sequentially; proper sequential multiplication gives 16.7%, so Choice C is correct, not D.",
