    "CorrectChoice": "A",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "ASC 330 defines margin as (Sales minus COGS) divided by Sales and turnover as COGS divided by average inventory. Profit equals $4,200,000 minus $2,520,000 equals $1,680,000, margin $1,680,000 divided by $4,200,000 equals 40.0%. Average inventory ($420,000 plus $480,000) divided by 2 equals $450,000, turnover $2,520,000 divided by $450,000 equals 5.6. Business interpretation: CFO Adaeze Onuorah should tell the board Flash holds pricing power at 40% but trails industry turnover 6.2, implying overstocking. A common trap is using ending inventory only, giving 5.25 and hiding the average investment.",
