    "UniqueConceptKey": "A-416-financial-leverage-evaluation",
    "Stem": "Adaeze Onuorah, CFO of Flash Manufacturing, is evaluating a proposal to replace $1,000,000 of equity financing with debt carrying a 10% interest rate. Flash currently expects EBIT of $1,200,000, pays interest of $150,000, faces a 30% tax rate, and has 200,000 shares outstanding. If the swap is executed, annual interest rises to $250,000 and Flash repurchases 25% of its shares with the proceeds. Assuming EBIT remains at $1,200,000, what is the effect on EPS, and what is the most appropriate conclusion for Adaeze?",
