    "UniqueConceptKey": "A-418-defensive-interval-ratio",
    "Stem": "Mariela Hoffmann, controller of Flash Manufacturing, is assessing how long the company could operate on its most liquid assets if cash inflows stopped. At year-end, Flash holds cash of $450,000, short-term marketable securities of $300,000, and net accounts receivable of $600,000. Flash's average daily operating expenditures, excluding noncash charges such as depreciation, are $75,000. What is Flash's defensive interval ratio in days?",
