    "ExplanationWrongB": "Choice B (conservative) over-insures. Holding large cash and marketable-security buffers financed with long-term debt eliminates liquidity risk but locks up capital earning returns below Flash's cost of capital, deepening the return-on-assets shortfall that is already below industry average. The liquidity protection is real, but the cost is disproportionate to the actual risk Flash faces.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
