    "ExplanationWrongC": "Choice C (legal sale = accounting sale) conflates legal form with economic substance. Financial reporting looks through legal form to substance: even if the documents call it a sale, the retention of risk through recourse means the accounting treatment must reflect a borrowing.",
    "ExplanationWrongD": "Choice D (no effect) is incorrect. Flash received cash and incurred an obligation to repay if collections fall short; the transaction changes Flash's financial position by converting receivables into cash plus a liability, which affects leverage and liquidity measures.",
