    "ExplanationWrongA": "Choice A (2.50) divides contribution margin by fixed costs: $5,000,000 / $2,000,000 = 2.50. The DOL denominator is operating income (contribution margin minus fixed costs), not fixed costs themselves. Using fixed costs directly overstates the leverage effect.",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Choice B (0.40) divides fixed costs by contribution margin: $2,000,000 / $5,000,000 = 0.40. This inverts the DOL relationship and measures the fixed-cost proportion of contribution, not the sensitivity of operating income to sales changes.",
    "ExplanationWrongC": "",
